<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="227c" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>The customer's SPE container id reaches the BFF as plain H4b settings from H8 (no vault); H13 I4 checks it (plan G18)</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T227 (gap G18)</phase>
    <gate>after 227b</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>L2 handler code, manifest/catalog generator contract, DAG edge, contract tests.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Follows the existing written-by-h3 precedent end to end.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <tags>provisioning, provisioning-handler, l2-controlplane, spe, key-vault, model1-dedicated, testing</tags>
    <deps>227b</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Give SPE-DefaultContainerId and SPE-CommunicationArchiveContainerId a real writer (H8), so a fresh stamp is not quarantined by H4 and the BFF gets both container ids.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (L2 control plane, canonical secret catalog). Follow the provisioning constraints.</role>

  <goal>
    The manifest marks both secrets written by H8; H4 and the generated seed script skip them; H8 writes both (the one container
    it creates) to the customer vault after verifying the container; H9 waits for H8 so the BFF boots with resolvable KV
    references; the email container setting uses the key the BFF reads (EmailProcessing__DefaultContainerId);
    RunContextContractTests.PinnedManifestGaps is empty.
  </goal>

  <justification>
    <existing>manifest value_source from-bicep-output (nothing produces it — KvSecretValueResolver always fails it → H4 PARTIAL → QuarantineRequired); written-by-h3 precedent (KvSecretValueSource.WrittenByEntraAppReg, H4 filter, generator skip, contract rule (g), GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner SetSecretAsync).</existing>
    <extension>Generalise the written-by-handler source to H8 (sibling enum value + filter + rule); H8 reuses H3's per-call SecretClient pattern.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Every fresh stamp is quarantined at H4 (G18); Communication:ArchiveContainerId is unset so CommunicationService throws; Email__DefaultContainerId is a dead key (BFF reads EmailProcessing:DefaultContainerId).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <context>
    <background>
      Fact sheet 2026-10-06: manifest.yaml :291-317 (app settings Email__DefaultContainerId — dead — and Communication__ArchiveContainerId);
      customer.bicep :780-785 omits both (cites G18); SecretClientKvWriter.cs :231-245; H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs :83, :476-487;
      DagAdvancer.cs :141-165 (H9←H3,H4b — not H8; H7←H6,H8,H9); H8 creates ONE container → InterStepState.SpeContainerId;
      RunContextContractTests.cs :504-505 pins both, positive control :576/:584 uses SPE-DefaultContainerId→T227.
      Adjacent (fix here): H13 I4 probe (SpeContainerTenantDerivationInvariantProbe.cs :218, :570-624) requires
      SharePointEmbedded__ContainerTypeId to be a KV reference, but H4b writes it as a literal GUID (not a secret) → I4 fails on
      every stamp. Accept the literal (the GUID is not secret); keep the check that it equals the run's containerTypeId.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml + Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 + generated/*</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecrets/** (FileKvSecretManifest, KvSecretValueResolver, H4 handler)</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SpeContainer/H8SpeContainerHandler.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Reconciler/DagAdvancer.cs</file>
      <file>H13 SpeContainerTenantDerivationInvariantProbe.cs</file>
      <file>Tests: RunContextContractTests, FileKvSecretManifestTests, H4/H8/H13 handler tests, DAG tests</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <decisions>
    <decision date="2026-10-06" by="owner (D28)">One container type per model, one container per customer (per Dataverse environment) — both container settings name H8's one container.</decision>
    <decision date="2026-10-06" by="agent, from evidence (deviation from constraint 'precedent' and steps 1-3)">No Key Vault at all: a container id is not a secret. Both secrets leave the catalog and become per_env_settings (from-h8-output:spe_container_id) that H4b writes, with H4b ← H8 in the DAG — the T242/T245b/T246 plain-setting precedent. This removes the written-by-h8 source, H8's vault write and its overwrite rule, which were needed only because the value was put in the vault. H9 still waits for H8 (H9 ← H4b ← H8).</decision>
  </decisions>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="precedent">Mirror written-by-h3 exactly (manifest value, enum, H4 filter, generator skip, contract rule). No special case inside H4.</constraint>
    <constraint source="KV">Never delete or overwrite a different existing value silently: if a secret exists with another value, fail Resumable naming it (upgrade safety).</constraint>
    <constraint source="DAG">Add H9 ← H8; DAG test updated.</constraint>
    <constraint source="catalog">Regenerate generated/* and run -Verify; re-verify after the pre-commit prettier pass.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Manifest + catalog: written-by-h8 for both; app setting key EmailProcessing__DefaultContainerId; regenerate.</step>
    <step order="2">Parser/enum/H4 filter/contract rule; remove both PinnedManifestGaps pins; re-seed the positive control with a synthetic name.</step>
    <step order="3">H8 KV writes (+ tests); DAG H9 ← H8.</step>
    <step order="4">H13 I4 probe accepts a literal container-type id equal to the run's containerTypeId (+ test).</step>
    <step order="5">Docs (inventory, plan G18/T227 ✅, CHANGELOG if .claude touched); verify; Step 9.5; close.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The manifest has neither container-id secret, so H4 cannot attempt or quarantine on them; H4b writes both settings from H8's SpeContainerId (H4b catalog test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DAG test: H4b (and so H9) waits for H8.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">RunContextContractTests.PinnedManifestGaps is empty; the positive control still proves the scanner flags an unwired secret.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">I4 probe tests: the run's container type + H8's container in both settings passes; another container fails CATASTROPHIC; missing / blank / other container type fails; run values missing is InfraFault.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Catalog -Verify OK; ControlPlane.Tests, Worker build, ArchTests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    COMPLETED 2026-10-06 (FULL).
    - manifest.yaml: SPE-DefaultContainerId + SPE-CommunicationArchiveContainerId removed from secrets; per_env_settings
      EmailProcessing__DefaultContainerId (the key the BFF reads — Email__DefaultContainerId was dead) and
      Communication__ArchiveContainerId from from-h8-output:spe_container_id. Catalog regenerated (-Verify OK); generated
      kv-secrets module and customer.json recompiled without the two secrets; generator allow-list + PerEnvSourceCatalog.
    - DAG: H4b ← H8 (H9 transitively). HandlerRunInputs H4b += SpeContainerId. RunContextContractTests: PinnedManifestGaps
      empty; positive control re-seeded with a synthetic pinned gap.
    - H13 I4 (SpeContainerTenantDerivationInvariantProbe) rewritten: it required SharePointEmbedded__ContainerTypeId to be a
      KV reference (H4b writes a literal — every stamp would fail) and never checked the customer's container. Now it
      compares: container type = the run's; both container settings = H8's container (another id = CATASTROPHIC, D28).
      InvariantVerificationRequest gained optional ContainerTypeId / SpeContainerId; H13 passes them.
    - Tests: DagAdvancerTests (H4b waits for H8), H4bBulkAppSettingsHandlerTests (catalog row), probe tests rewritten.
      ControlPlane.Tests 2124/0/1.
    - Docs: inventory SPE rows, plan G18, manifest-driven-secret-catalog pattern rule 4, customer.bicep comment.
    - Legacy scripts Configure-ProductionAppSettings.ps1 / Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1 (retired shared production stack):
      marked LEGACY; the dead Email__DefaultContainerId key fixed to EmailProcessing__DefaultContainerId.
    - Step 9.5: adr-check 0 violations — W1 spec FR-31 / design §4D I4 wording amended (container id = stamp app settings,
      verified by H13); W2 resolver bypass (BFF reads EmailProcessing:DefaultContainerId directly; ITenantContainerResolver
